        "question": "How do you implement JWT authentication with secure token renewal?",
        "answer": "Secure JWT authentication uses short-lived access tokens (5-15 mins) stored in memory and long-lived refresh tokens (7-30 days) stored in secure, HttpOnly, SameSite cookies. When the access token expires, the client makes an automated refresh call to a dedicated endpoint that validates the refresh token against a database session table, checks for revocation, and issues a freshly signed access token. This limits the blast radius of stolen tokens.",
