        "id": "healthtech-medical-informatics-int-31",
        "questionNumber": 31,
        "level": "Intermediate",
        "category": "Performance Optimization & Caching",
        "question": "Explain the concept of connection pooling in databases and why it is critical for backend scale.",
        "answer": "Database connection establishment involves expensive network round trips, TLS handshakes, and process allocation on the database server. Connection pooling maintains a pre-allocated cache of active database connections that worker threads borrow and return. This prevents connection thrashing, limits database memory spikes, and allows a pool of 20-50 connections to serve thousands of concurrent web requests efficiently.",
        "keyTakeaways": [
          "Explains the overhead of TCP/TLS connection handshakes",
          "Describes connection pool mechanics and sizing formulas",
          "Understands resource protection on the database server"
        ]
