        "question": "How does HTTP/HTTPS communication work between client and server?",
        "answer": "HTTP is a stateless application layer protocol operating over TCP/IP. The client sends a request consisting of a method (GET, POST, PUT, DELETE), headers, and optional body. The server processes the request and responds with a status code (200 OK, 400 Bad Request, 500 Server Error) and payload. HTTPS adds TLS/SSL encryption, securing the transport layer against eavesdropping and tampering via asymmetric key handshakes.",
