        "question": "How do you diagnose and resolve a severe memory leak in a production runtime environment?",
        "answer": "Diagnosing a production memory leak involves: 1) Inspecting APM heap telemetry to observe the sawtooth memory pattern failing to reclaim baseline memory after GC; 2) Capturing a heap dump using V8/JVM profiler during elevated memory; 3) Comparing consecutive heap snapshots in Chrome DevTools or Eclipse Memory Analyzer (MAT) to identify retained object dominator trees; 4) Pinpointing common root causes like unclosed database streams, global event listener leaks, or unbounded cache maps; 5) Deploying a targeted fix with automated leak regression tests.",
